<!--Post: 6863--><!--Time: 1108054597-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6863"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 8:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Im trying understand the history of the Otero family prior to the murders. where they lived, who they knew, what they did, etc. i believe the key to the case lies there. Would someone mind summarizing what we know??? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6863-->
<!--Post: 6997--><!--Time: 1108114481-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6997"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 1:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Check Charley&#39;s interview.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6997-->
<!--Post: 7061--><!--Time: 1108160675-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7061"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 2:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->They lived in camden, NJ for a while before comming to kansas. There were 5 children, the 3 children who lived went to New Mexico to live with a family friend after the murders. Prior to the murders, the family got a new washing machine &amp; Dryer also I think delivered a few days before. <BR>I think the mom was not working or the dad when the crimes happened, they olny lived in the house in W , kansas for about a year.I think they lived in a differnt town in kansas before moving to W. <BR> They had a big dog, lucky, a part shepard who barked a lot but the mom was realy close to him, he would follow the mom around the house. Lucky was walked by the children and they did have a fence at there house.I hope this info helps.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7061-->
<!--Post: 8289--><!--Time: 1109039424-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8289"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 6:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i am particularly interested in whether there was a NM connection in the otero&#39;s past prior to the murder. i know charlie ended up there after, but what about before? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8289-->
<!--Post: 8338--><!--Time: 1109063101-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8338"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 1:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve looked for one too, but are a LOT of Oteros in New Mexico. It&#39;s a good bet, though, that if a family friend either lived there, or moved there, there&#39;s a connection. <BR> <BR> Write yourself a paragraph explaining why you think there is a connection. Then underline all of the keywords. Then Google: New Mexico Otero [keyword] <BR> <BR>You might find something to go on.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
